			"Message": "fix(Output): Restore eager paint and re-enable webview panel service injection\n\nRevert the `DisableLazyPaint` opt-in gate to restore unconditional requestAnimationFrame and IntersectionObserver overrides. The previous gating (`__LAND_AGGRESSIVE_LAZY_PAINT__`) regressed editor mount behavior—preventing the editor from loading until user interaction—because WKWebView's compositor does not fire native callbacks on hidden surfaces. Restoring the overrides ensures immediate paint and layout resolution without relying on user clicks.\n\nRe-introduce the `.monaco-workbench .part { isolation: isolate; }` CSS rule in `PartZIndexCSS`. While this rule previously blocked input events under WKWebView, that issue was resolved by the `ForceTextAreaInput` fix in recent commits. The `isolation` property is now required to prevent `transform: translate3d` hints from promoting individual parts into new stacking contexts, which was hiding sibling layers.\n\nAugment the `ExposeWorkbenchAccessor` transform to inject `IWebviewWorkbenchService`. This service is required by `SkyBridge` to materialize real editor-based panels for `vscode.window.createWebviewPanel` calls (e.g., Roo chat, Claude surfaces). Without this injection, such webviews were silently parked in memory and never rendered. The service is now exposed alongside `IWebviewViewService` and other core workbench services via the `__CEL_SERVICES__` facade.",
			"SHA": "cc92003ba07d5af70491041752a39a3b4ebebe0a"
		}
	],
